te answer 01-047: Overfitting — how prevent it? — train-val gap diagnostic, 5-lever prevention toolkit (data/L2/dropout/early-stopping/model-simplification), QLoRA rank constraint as regularization, double-descent caveat for LLMs\n2026-06-16 | 01-llm-fundamentals | wrote answer 01-048: Imbalanced datasets — how handle? — three-layer mitigation (metrics: PR-AUC over accuracy; algorithm: class_weight/focal loss; data: SMOTE/LLM augmentation), threshold tuning via PR curve, production monitoring for imbalance drift\n2026-06-16 | 01-llm-fundamentals | validate PASSED — all 49 files OK (1 category overview + 48 answer notes)\n2026-06-16 | scaffold | queued 02-rag-systems (36 tasks)\n2026-06-16 | 02-rag-systems | wrote category overview: 34-question checklist, 4 sub-topics (pipeline/chunking, retrieval architecture, evaluation, production scaling), decision framework covering retrieval strategy + chunking + eval + RAG-vs-alternatives, 6 common mistakes, one-page summary\n2026-06-16 | 02-rag-systems | wrote answer 02-001: Design a RAG system for a customer support chatbot — 9-stage pipeline (ingest→chunk→embed→index→hybrid-retrieve→cross-encoder-rerank→generate→RAGAS-evaluate→observe), concrete stack (Pinecone+ES BM25+RRF+Cohere Rerank+GPT-4o-mini), production metrics (cost/query, deflection rate, p95 latency), golden dataset eval framework\n2026-06-16 | 02-rag-systems | wrote answer 02-002: How would you design an LLM-powered enterprise search system? — multi-source ACL-aware RAG, connector federation (Confluence/Slack/GitHub/Salesforce), ACL enforcement at vector retrieval layer, query-type segmentation (navigation vs factual vs exploratory), hybrid search + cross-encoder reranking, freshness boost for real-time sources, golden dataset + click-signal quality loop\n2026-06-16 | 02-rag-systems | wrote answer 02-003: Design a GenAI document-processing pipeline for unstructured data — MIME-type routing (PyMuPDF/Textract/email parser), structure-aware extraction (tables→Markdown, OCR confidence gating), parent-child chunking (1024/256 tokens), metadata-rich indexing (Pinecone+ES BM25), GPT-4o vision for charts, cost-routing heuristic (native text → free parser; scanned → Textract)\n2026-06-16 | 02-rag-systems | wrote answer 02-004: How would you use GPT-4 to generate accurate answers from proprietary documents? — RAG pipeline (hybrid BM25+dense retrieval → cross-encoder rerank → grounding prompt T=0 + citations), cost table at 1M queries/day (~$2.5K/day vs $50K+ for full-context approach), faithfulness gate for strict accuracy, golden dataset eval framework\n2026-06-16 | 02-rag-systems | wrote answer 02-005: Design a generative QA assistant for your company's knowledge base — ACL-aware hybrid RAG pipeline (Confluence/Notion connectors, webhook freshness, BM25+dense RRF fusion, cross-encoder rerank, grounding prompt T=0 with citations), model tiering (GPT-4o-mini vs GPT-4o), RAGAS golden-dataset eval gate, deflection-rate production SLO\n2026-06-16 | 02-rag-systems | wrote answer 02-006: System processing huge PDF reports — structure-aware extraction (PyMuPDF/Textract), global metadata injection (currency units as chunk fields + generation preamble), parent-child chunking (1024/256 tokens), table-as-unit handling, overlap windows\n2026-06-16 | 02-rag-systems | wrote answer 02-007: How efficiently generate and store embeddings for products and queries? — offline batch pipeline (2048/call async, OpenAI ~$20/5M products), Pinecone/Qdrant vector storage with metadata sidecar, CDC-driven incremental updates via Debezium+Kafka, same model rule for index vs query, MRL dimension truncation and self-hosting break-even\n2026-06-16 | 02-rag-systems | wrote answer 02-008: How handle hallucination when no information is found in context? — defense-in-depth stack: cosine-similarity retrieval gate (θ≈0.70 short-circuits before LLM call), grounding prompt at T=0 with explicit abstention instruction, RAGAS faithfulness post-check (<0.8 → replace with canned response), production monitoring of abstention vs hallucination rates separately\n2026-06-16 | 02-rag-systems | wrote answer 02-009: What RAG projects have you worked on? — STAR+Tradeoffs walkthrough framework, parent-child chunking + hybrid RRF + Cohere rerank example, deflection-rate failure arc, 3 concrete pitfalls about tool-naming vs tradeoff ownership\n2026-06-16 | 02-rag-systems | wrote answer 02-010: Design a Q&A system over internal documentation — ACL-enforced RAG pipeline with Confluence/Notion/GitHub connectors, hybrid BM25+dense retrieval with RRF, cross-encoder reranking, per-user Okta group filtering at retrieval layer, GPT-4o-mini with grounding prompt T=0 and citation links, RAGAS golden-dataset eval\n2026-06-16 | 02-rag-systems | wrote answer 02-011: How ensure quality of data the LLM interacts with? — 3-layer quality framework (ingestion: schema+dedup+PII+chunk hygiene; retrieval: cosine threshold+cross-encoder reranking; post-gen: RAGAS faithfulness gate+drift monitoring), BGE-Reranker precision@5 61%→78% example, Presidio PII scrubbing, MinHash near-dedup\n2026-06-16 | 02-rag-systems | wrote answer 02-012: Compare sparse vs dense retrieval — BM25 inverted-index exact-match vs bi-encoder HNSW semantic retrieval, failure modes table, RRF hybrid fusion (Elasticsearch 8.9+), cross-encoder reranking; when to use each and production default\n2026-06-16 | 02-rag-systems | wrote answer 02-013: Common RAG failure points — how debug them? — 6-mode taxonomy (bad chunking, vocab mismatch, lost-in-middle, hallucination-on-absent-context, stale index, weak eval), RAGAS split protocol (context_recall vs faithfulness), systematic debug decision tree, real incident pattern (SKU dense-only failure → BM25 hybrid fix)\n2026-06-16 | 02-rag-systems | wrote answer 02-014: How protect sensitive/confidential data in a RAG pipeline? — 5-layer defense-in-depth (Presidio PII redaction at ingestion, ACL metadata on chunks, per-user group filter at retrieval, post-gen Presidio scan, PII-redacted logs), pseudonymization vs redaction tradeoff, async PII scanning at scale\n2026-06-16 | 02-rag-systems | wrote answer 02-015: What vector databases have you used? Which and why? — 5-axis selection framework (managed/scale/filtering/latency/cost), Pinecone vs Qdrant vs Weaviate vs pgvector vs FAISS comparison table, pre-filtering vs post-filtering recall tradeoff, production migration example (Pinecone→Qdrant for ACL filters), cost modeling at 1M QPS\n2026-06-16 | 02-rag-systems | wrote answer 02-016: Financial report 'amounts in thousands' — doc-wide context handling via metadata extraction pass (PyMuPDF/Textract + GPT-4o-mini), parent-child chunking with amounts_unit/period/entity fields on every chunk, generation preamble injection, per-section unit override schema for conflicting declarations\n2026-06-16 | 02-rag-systems | wrote answer 02-017: What is hybrid search? When combine vector + BM25? — RRF fusion of BM25 inverted index (exact keyword recall) + bi-encoder HNSW (semantic recall), rank-based normalization, Elasticsearch 8.9+ native hybrid, cross-encoder reranking layer, SKU failure mode fix (Recall@5 61%→79%)\n2026-06-16 | 02-rag-systems | wrote answer 02-018: What is re-ranking? Cross-encoder vs bi-encoder? — two-stage retrieve-then-rerank architecture, bi-encoder (independent encoding, ANN, pre-indexable) vs cross-encoder (joint query+doc cross-attention, query-time only, top-N candidates), Cohere Rerank / BGE-Reranker / ms-marco tooling, ~80-200ms latency cost for 20-30pt precision gain, NDCG evaluation angle\n2026-06-16 | 02-rag-systems | wrote answer 02-019: Scale RAG to 10M+ articles — horizontal shard fan-out (5M vectors/shard, scatter-gather merge), 3-layer caching (embedding→semantic→response, GPTCache), staged retrieval (ANN top-100→BM25 top-20→cross-encoder top-5), CDC-driven incremental ingestion, speculative shard timeout pattern, cost comparison Pinecone vs self-hosted Qdrant at scale\n2026-06-16 | 02-rag-systems | wrote answer 02-020: RAG returns relevant docs but users can't find the answer — search engine vs answer engine; RAGAS context_recall vs answer_relevancy diagnostic split, context dumping / lost-in-middle / query reformulation gap failure modes, synthesis prompt fix + top-k reduction + graceful fallback pattern\n2026-06-16 | 02-rag-systems | wrote answer 02-021: How evaluate a RAG pipeline? — two-layer eval (retrieval: Recall@5/MRR/NDCG/Precision@k on golden dataset; generation: RAGAS Faithfulness/Answer Relevancy/Context Precision/Context Recall), golden dataset regression gates, production signals (deflection rate, p95 latency, thumbs-down), BLEU/ROUGE pitfall, cost tradeoff gpt-4o vs gpt-4o-mini judge\n2026-06-16 | 02-rag-systems | wrote answer 02-022: Citations and source attribution in RAG — metadata-at-ingestion pipeline, numbered source-block prompting, NLI entailment citation validation (DeBERTa, <0.75 threshold), structured JSON citation response for frontend rendering\n2026-06-16 | 02-rag-systems | wrote answer 02-023: How does ANN search work? HNSW indexing? — layered skip-graph construction, O(log N) greedy descent, M/ef_construction/ef_search parameter guide, FAISS IVF+PQ vs HNSW tradeoff, filtered-search recall-collapse pitfall, Pinecone/Qdrant/FAISS tooling\n2026-06-16 | 02-rag-systems | wrote answer 02-024: Where do embeddings fail? — negation (polarity ignored by contrastive training, cosine>0.85 between X and not-X), temporal/exact-match precision (BPE fragments rare strings, no time axis, metadata filter mitigation), conjunctive queries; mitigations: BM25 hybrid search + RRF, cross-encoder reranking, structured metadata filters\n2026-06-16 | 02-rag-systems | wrote answer 02-025: Semantic caching — reduce cost and latency — three-layer caching stack (response/embedding/retrieval cache), GPTCache/FAISS/Redis mechanics, cosine similarity threshold tuning (0.92–0.97), TTL+invalidation strategy, cost math at 1M queries/day (30% hit rate = $3K/day saved